  "description": "ASISUS crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H70 N6 O20 Sm4,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm1A (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2A (Sm) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.598-3.967 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.30-110.96°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H70N6O20Sm4·2(C2H3N). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
